# Bluetooth LE keyboards and mice (HID over GATT) reach the kernel through
# bluetoothd, which creates their input device by opening /dev/uhid.
# 70-sunstone.rules (from Android's ueventd.rc) makes /dev/uhid 0660
# 3011:3011, and bluetoothd runs as root with only CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE (bluetooth.service), so without CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE it
# cannot open it: LE keyboards connected but typed nothing. Make root the
# owner; Android's uhid group (3011) keeps its access.
# See docs/roadmap-hardware-2.md, Bluetooth pairings and LE keyboards.
ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="uhid", OWNER="0"
